IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja1-part3-div4`

-- Tests for scja1-part3-div4.l4 (ss 19 to 22B). Expected values are written from the text (SCJA1969.txt lines 1673-1880), not from the code.

§ `Fixtures`

`no split of opinion` MEANS `Split of opinion` OF 0, 0

-- A civil decision of a given court with a given amount in dispute (MAYBE NUMBER).
GIVEN `lower court` IS A Court
      amount IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A Decision
`a civil decision` MEANS Decision OF `lower court`, `appellate jurisdiction`, `a civil proceeding`, `any other civil matter`, (Order OF `another order or application`, `granted unconditionally`), TRUE, FALSE, amount, (Date 1 6 2024), NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE

-- A hearing in which oral evidence is given or not, and all the parties consent or not.
GIVEN oral IS A BOOLEAN
      consent IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Hearing
`a civil hearing` MEANS Hearing OF (Bench OF `General Division`, EMPTY), `in open court`, `a civil proceeding`, oral, consent, FALSE, `no split of opinion`

§§ `s 19: appellate criminal jurisdiction`

-- inputs: the matter, the hearing is before one or more Judges according to criminal procedure
#ASSERT (`s 19 the appellate criminal jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the matter` `s 19(a) an appeal from a District Court or Magistrate's Court` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 19 the appellate criminal jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the matter` `s 19(a) an appeal from a District Court or Magistrate's Court` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 19 the appellate criminal jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the matter` `s 19(b) a point of law reserved by a special case submitted by a District Court or Magistrate's Court` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 19 the appellate criminal jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the matter` `s 19(b) a point of law reserved by a special case submitted by a District Court or Magistrate's Court` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 19 the appellate criminal jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the matter` `s 19(ba) a review of an order of a District Court or Magistrate's Court in extradition proceedings` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 19 the appellate criminal jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the matter` `s 19(c) an appeal from a Family Court when exercising criminal jurisdiction` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 19 the appellate criminal jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the matter` `s 19(d) an appeal from a Youth Court` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a matter under none of the paragraphs: the section has no "only"
#ASSERT (`s 19 the appellate criminal jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the matter` `s 19 another matter` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 20: appellate civil jurisdiction`

-- inputs: the lower court, the nature of the case, a written law prescribes an appeal from the tribunal
#ASSERT (`s 20 the appellate civil jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the appeal` `Family Court` `a civil proceeding` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 20 the appellate civil jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the appeal` `Family Court` `a quasi-criminal proceeding` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 20 the appellate civil jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the appeal` `District Court` `a civil proceeding` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 20 the appellate civil jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the appeal` `Magistrate's Court` `a quasi-criminal proceeding` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a criminal case from these courts is s 19's, not s 20's
#ASSERT (`s 20 the appellate civil jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the appeal` `District Court` `a criminal proceeding` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 20 the appellate civil jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the appeal` `Family Court` `a criminal proceeding` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (c): another tribunal, if a written law prescribes the appeal
#ASSERT (`s 20 the appellate civil jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the appeal` `another subordinate court, tribunal or judicial or quasi-judicial body` `a civil proceeding` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 20 the appellate civil jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the appeal` `another subordinate court, tribunal or judicial or quasi-judicial body` `a civil proceeding` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 20 the appellate civil jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the appeal` `Youth Court` `a civil proceeding` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 21: appeals from District Courts and Magistrates' Courts`

-- (1)(a): the Act's own figure is $60,000: at the figure, within; one dollar over, outside
#ASSERT (`s 21(1)(a) the amount in dispute or the value of the subject matter does not exceed the sum` (`a civil decision` `District Court` (JUST 60000)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 21(1)(a) the amount in dispute or the value of the subject matter does not exceed the sum` (`a civil decision` `District Court` (JUST 59999)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 21(1)(a) the amount in dispute or the value of the subject matter does not exceed the sum` (`a civil decision` `District Court` (JUST 60001)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 21(1)(a) the amount in dispute or the value of the subject matter does not exceed the sum` (`a civil decision` `Magistrate's Court` (JUST 0)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an order under (3) raising the figure to $100,000 and one lowering it to $50,000
#ASSERT (`s 21(1)(a) the amount in dispute or the value of the subject matter does not exceed the sum` (`a civil decision` `District Court` (JUST 80000)) (JUST 100000)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 21(1)(a) the amount in dispute or the value of the subject matter does not exceed the sum` (`a civil decision` `District Court` (JUST 100001)) (JUST 100000)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 21(1)(a) the amount in dispute or the value of the subject matter does not exceed the sum` (`a civil decision` `District Court` (JUST 55000)) (JUST 50000)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no amount or value: the Act does not say how an unvalued case counts
#ASSERT (`s 21(1)(a) the amount in dispute or the value of the subject matter does not exceed the sum` (`a civil decision` `District Court` NOTHING) NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1), the twin: is this a case in which an appeal needs permission? inputs: the decision, the order's amount, seam 3 (the Third Schedule)
#ASSERT (`s 21(1) permission is needed to appeal from the decision` (`a civil decision` `District Court` (JUST 60000)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 21(1) permission is needed to appeal from the decision` (`a civil decision` `District Court` (JUST 60001)) NOTHING (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- over the figure and not in the Third Schedule: outside both cases, the subsection does not speak
#ASSERT (`s 21(1) permission is needed to appeal from the decision` (`a civil decision` `District Court` (JUST 60001)) NOTHING (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 21(1) permission is needed to appeal from the decision` (`a civil decision` `District Court` (JUST 60001)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the Third Schedule's answer is not given and the amount is not decided either
#ASSERT (`s 21(1) permission is needed to appeal from the decision` (`a civil decision` `District Court` NOTHING) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1): inputs are the decision, the order's amount, seam 3, permission from the lower court, permission from the General Division
-- a case needing permission, permission from the lower court: the appeal lies
#ASSERT (`s 21(1) an appeal lies to the General Division from the decision` (`a civil decision` `District Court` (JUST 1000)) NOTHING NOTHING TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- permission from the General Division
#ASSERT (`s 21(1) an appeal lies to the General Division from the decision` (`a civil decision` `Magistrate's Court` (JUST 1000)) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "only with the permission": none given
#ASSERT (`s 21(1) an appeal lies to the General Division from the decision` (`a civil decision` `District Court` (JUST 1000)) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a Third Schedule case without permission
#ASSERT (`s 21(1) an appeal lies to the General Division from the decision` (`a civil decision` `District Court` (JUST 100000)) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a Third Schedule case with permission
#ASSERT (`s 21(1) an appeal lies to the General Division from the decision` (`a civil decision` `District Court` (JUST 100000)) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- outside both cases: the subsection says nothing about whether an appeal lies
#ASSERT (`s 21(1) an appeal lies to the General Division from the decision` (`a civil decision` `District Court` (JUST 100000)) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 21(1) an appeal lies to the General Division from the decision` (`a civil decision` `District Court` (JUST 100000)) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a decision of some other court is not within the subsection
#ASSERT (`s 21(1) an appeal lies to the General Division from the decision` (`a civil decision` `Family Court` (JUST 1000)) NOTHING NOTHING TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2A) and (3)
#ASSERT (`s 21(2A) the order is final` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 21(2A) the order is final` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 21(3) the President may vary the amount mentioned in section 21(1)` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 21(3) the President may vary the amount mentioned in section 21(1)` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 21(3) the President may vary the amount mentioned in section 21(1)` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 21(3) the President may vary the amount mentioned in section 21(1)` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 22: powers of rehearing`

#ASSERT (`s 22(1) the appeal is by way of rehearing` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22(1) the appeal is by way of rehearing` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 22(2) the General Division has the power or duty` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22(2) the General Division has the power or duty` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 22(2) the General Division has the power or duty` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): further evidence, the four ways
#ASSERT (`s 22(3) the General Division may receive further evidence in this manner` `s 22(3)(a) by oral examination in court` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22(3) the General Division may receive further evidence in this manner` `s 22(3)(b) by affidavit` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22(3) the General Division may receive further evidence in this manner` `s 22(3)(c) by deposition taken before an examiner or a commissioner` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22(3) the General Division may receive further evidence in this manner` `s 22(3)(d) in any other manner` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22(3) the General Division may receive further evidence in this manner` `s 22(3)(d) in any other manner` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): matters occurring after the date of the decision (decision made 10 June 2024)
#ASSERT (`s 22(5) the further evidence may be given to the General Division without permission` (Date 11 6 2024) (Date 10 6 2024)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22(5) the further evidence may be given to the General Division without permission` (Date 10 6 2024) (Date 10 6 2024)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 22(5) the further evidence may be given to the General Division without permission` (Date 9 6 2024) (Date 10 6 2024)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4): inputs are the date the matters occurred, the decision's date, permission given, special grounds
-- matters after the decision: no permission or special grounds needed
#ASSERT (`s 22(4) the further evidence may be given to the General Division` (Date 11 6 2024) (Date 10 6 2024) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- matters on or before the decision date: permission AND special grounds
#ASSERT (`s 22(4) the further evidence may be given to the General Division` (Date 9 6 2024) (Date 10 6 2024) TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22(4) the further evidence may be given to the General Division` (Date 9 6 2024) (Date 10 6 2024) TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 22(4) the further evidence may be given to the General Division` (Date 9 6 2024) (Date 10 6 2024) FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 22(4) the further evidence may be given to the General Division` (Date 10 6 2024) (Date 10 6 2024) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (6), (7)
#ASSERT (`s 22(6) the General Division may draw the inference, give the judgment or make the order` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22(6) the General Division may draw the inference, give the judgment or make the order` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 22(7)(a) the power may be exercised in relation to any part of the decision appealed against` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22(7)(a) the power may be exercised in relation to any part of the decision appealed against` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 22(7)(b) the power may be exercised in favour of any party to the decision appealed against` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22(7)(b) the power may be exercised in favour of any party to the decision appealed against` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 22A: oral hearing not needed for appellate matters`

-- (1): inputs are appellate civil jurisdiction, matter prescribed by the Rules
#ASSERT (`s 22A(1) the General Division may decide the matter without hearing oral arguments` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22A(1) the General Division may decide the matter without hearing oral arguments` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 22A(1) the General Division may decide the matter without hearing oral arguments` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): oral evidence in the part, consent of all the parties
#ASSERT (`s 22A(2) section 22A(1) allows this part of the proceeding to be conducted without an oral hearing` (`a civil hearing` TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 22A(2) section 22A(1) allows this part of the proceeding to be conducted without an oral hearing` (`a civil hearing` TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22A(2) section 22A(1) allows this part of the proceeding to be conducted without an oral hearing` (`a civil hearing` FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 22A(3) the General Division may direct that the matter be heard in an asynchronous manner by exchange of written correspondence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22A(3) the General Division may direct that the matter be heard in an asynchronous manner by exchange of written correspondence` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 22A(4) the General Division must not hear the matter in an asynchronous manner` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22A(4) the General Division must not hear the matter in an asynchronous manner` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 22A(5) section 22A affects the General Division's power to hear oral arguments before deciding the matter` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 22A(5) section 22A affects the General Division's power to hear oral arguments before deciding the matter` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- The regulative rule for (4), run: a General Division that hears the matter asynchronously when that is inconsistent with its duty of fairness is in BREACH; one that takes some other step
-- is FULFILLED; where there is no inconsistency the rule is FULFILLED at once. (Read from the output of `l4 run`: BREACH, FULFILLED, FULFILLED.)
#TRACE `s 22A(4) the General Division shall not hear the matter in an asynchronous manner` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 22A(4) the General Division` DOES `s 22A(4) hears the matter in an asynchronous manner` AT 0
#TRACE `s 22A(4) the General Division shall not hear the matter in an asynchronous manner` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 22A(4) the General Division` DOES `s 22A(4) takes some other step in the matter` AT 5
#TRACE `s 22A(4) the General Division shall not hear the matter in an asynchronous manner` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 22A(4) the General Division` DOES `s 22A(4) hears the matter in an asynchronous manner` AT 0

§§ `s 22B: summary dismissal of certain appeals`

#ASSERT (`s 22B(3) the thing is an appeal for the purposes of section 22B` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22B(3) the thing is an appeal for the purposes of section 22B` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22B(3) the thing is an appeal for the purposes of section 22B` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1): inputs are the appellate civil jurisdiction condition, then limbs (a), (b), (c)
#ASSERT (`s 22B(1) the General Division may on its own motion summarily dismiss the appeal` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22B(1) the General Division may on its own motion summarily dismiss the appeal` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22B(1) the General Division may on its own motion summarily dismiss the appeal` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22B(1) the General Division may on its own motion summarily dismiss the appeal` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 22B(1) the General Division may on its own motion summarily dismiss the appeal` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)
#ASSERT (`s 22B(2) the General Division may summarily dismiss the appeal under section 22B(1) now, as the section requires` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 22B(2) the General Division may summarily dismiss the appeal under section 22B(1) now, as the section requires` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 22B(2) the General Division may summarily dismiss the appeal under section 22B(1) now, as the section requires` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- The regulative rule for (2), run. (Read from the output of `l4 run`: FULFILLED, a residual MUST, FULFILLED.)
#TRACE `s 22B(2) the General Division must give the appellant an opportunity to show cause and consider the representations` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 22B(2) the General Division` DOES `s 22B(2) gives the appellant a reasonable opportunity to show cause` AT 1
    PARTY `s 22B(2) the General Division` DOES `s 22B(2) considers the representations of the appellant` AT 2
#TRACE `s 22B(2) the General Division must give the appellant an opportunity to show cause and consider the representations` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 22B(2) the General Division` DOES `s 22B(2) gives the appellant a reasonable opportunity to show cause` AT 1
#TRACE `s 22B(2) the General Division must give the appellant an opportunity to show cause and consider the representations` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 22B(2) the General Division` DOES `s 22B(2) considers the representations of the appellant` AT 1
